Done. All seven steps are complete and verified against the saved artefacts on disk.

**What was built**

- `scripts/download_models.py` — pulls `FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base` and `dominguesm/xlm-roberta-base-lora-language-detection` (cache at `/root/hf_cache`, kept out of the repo).
- `scripts/setup_model.py` — loads the base as `XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification` with `num_labels=20` (+ the adapter's `id2label`/`label2id`), saves model and tokenizer to `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base`, applies the adapter with `PeftModel.from_pretrained`, then `merge_and_unload()` and saves to `/app/merged_model/`.
- `scripts/detect.py` — runs the 10 samples and writes `/app/detection_results.json` with exactly `text`, `predicted_class_id`, `confidence`; the class id is the raw argmax of the logits.
- `scripts/verify.py` — reloads both artefacts from disk and checks reproduction plus per-language accuracy.

**Key detail:** the adapter ships `adapter_model.bin` with a real 20-class classifier head in `modules_to_save`, so the 20-class config is what makes the adapter's head load instead of a randomly initialised 2-class one. Merging preserves the behaviour exactly — max logit difference pre/post merge was `4.4e-06` — and the merged checkpoint contains no `lora_*` keys and a `classifier.out_proj` of shape `(20, 768)`.

**The check**

`scripts/verify.py` reloads everything from disk: 10/10 saved predictions reproduce, and on a proxy set of 4 sentences per language across all 20 languages it scores 80/80 (100% overall, worst language 100%), well above the 95% overall / 75% per-language bar. The 10 requested samples all land on the right language with 0.94–1.00 confidence.

**Left undone:** nothing. One note — installing `transformers`/`torch`/`peft` was needed and came from PyPI (the sandbox blocks `curl`/`wget` but package managers reach the network), and the model weights stay in `/root/hf_cache` rather than the repo, which is why the download and setup scripts point there.

